{1 tiny_appkits }

What applications share, written from scratch for teaching: the
engines under the Tiny applications, one idea per module, each
interface explaining its idea. None of them draws with the
{{:../elm_playground/index.html} Elm Playground}: a document, a sheet, a
drawing, a model are values, and the application draws them (the kits
that draw, a File menu, compound documents, the browsers' drawing, are
the Playground's, beside the apps they help). They stand on
{{:../tiny_libs/index.html} tiny_libs} and
{{:../tiny_languages/index.html} tiny_languages}.

Each is a library of its own, named [tiny_appkits.<name>] outside this
repository, for example in a dune file:

{v
(executable
 (name main)
 (libraries tiny_appkits.appkit_sheet tiny_appkits.browser_layout))
v}

The libraries are unwrapped: their modules are used by their own names,
[Sheet.set], [Box_layout.layout].

{2:documents Documents}

A document as a value, its undo and its clipboard
([tiny_appkits.appkit_document]):

{!modules: Document Undo Clipboard Saved}

{2:office The office}

The spreadsheet's engine ([tiny_appkits.appkit_sheet]) and a sheet
drawn in a rectangle ([tiny_appkits.appkit_sheet_view]); diagrams whose
geometry is a sheet ([tiny_appkits.appkit_diagram]); text with looks,
laid out on pages ([tiny_appkits.appkit_richtext]); a paragraph broken
into lines, greedy or by Knuth and Plass ([tiny_appkits.appkit_typeset]);
a presentation as an outline ([tiny_appkits.appkit_slides]); NLS's tree
of statements ([tiny_appkits.appkit_nls]):

{!modules:
    Sheet Sheet_view Diagram Ortho_route
    Rich Style Page Flow Linebreak
    Outline Nls_doc
}

{2:graphics Pictures and drawings}

MacPaint's bitmap ([tiny_appkits.appkit_paint]), Deluxe Paint's colour
numbers and palette cycling ([tiny_appkits.appkit_indexed]), MacDraw's
figures ([tiny_appkits.appkit_draw]), a 3D modeller's scene
([tiny_appkits.appkit_modeler]):

{!modules:
    Bitmap Pattern Paint Seed_fill
    Indexed Cycling
    Figure Drawing
    Modeler Modeler_view
}

{2:cad CAD}

Sketchpad ([tiny_appkits.appkit_sketch]), AutoCAD
([tiny_appkits.appkit_cad]), SketchUp ([tiny_appkits.appkit_pushpull]):

{!modules:
    Sketch Relax
    Cad_geom Cad_drawing Cad_edit Cad_snap Cad_session Dxf
    Skp_model Skp_infer Skp_view Bsp
}

{2:text Text mode}

The editors as full-screen programs, vi, Emacs over its Lisp, Turbo
Pascal's IDE ([tiny_appkits.appkit_editor]); a full-screen game
([tiny_appkits.appkit_tui]); the teletype's games
([tiny_appkits.appkit_teletype]):

{!modules:
    Gap_buffer Emacs_editor Emacs_simple Tui_vi Tui_emacs Tui_turbo
    Tui_snake
    Tty_hangman Tty_guess Tty_wumpus
}

{2:programming Programming by blocks}

Where each block lies and where a dragged stack snaps
([tiny_appkits.appkit_blocks]):

{!modules: Block_layout Block_edit}

{2:web A web page's layout}

Blocks and lines, tables, CSS's box model and flexbox, and the way back
from a point to a link ([tiny_appkits.browser_layout]):

{!modules: Html_layout Table_layout Box_layout Flex_layout Hit}

{2:pim Time, the sky, money}

iCalendar and vCard ([tiny_appkits.appkit_pim]), a planetarium's
astronomy ([tiny_appkits.appkit_astronomy]), a checking account
([tiny_appkits.appkit_money]):

{!modules:
    Ics Vcard
    Celestial Ephemeris Bright_stars Stereographic
    Money Ledger Reconcile Qif
}
